                        <field name="dc_date">1866 </field>
                        <field name="dc_description">Cover page contains an illustration of an eagle carrying a harp with the inscription 'love one another'. -- Contains the constitution of the Fenian Brotherhood. -- Printer: N.Y. Printing Co., 81, 83 & 85 Centre Street., 40 Ann St. -- Includes a report of the finance committee of the Fenian Brotherhood. -- Includes a liist of resolutions unanimously passed at the first general Congress of the Fenian Brotherhood. -- This is the "Proceedings" of the group of the Fenian Brotherhood which broke away from the original group after President John O'Mahony was impeached at the 3rd National Congress, Philadelphia, Oct. 21, 1865. Cf. Savage, "Fenian heroes and martyrs", P. Donahoe, 1868. </field>
